> create Windows-compatible PowerShell hooks for prettier?

● Here are Windows-compatible PowerShell hooks for prettier:

  PreToolUse hook:
  powershell -Command "$j = [Console]::In.ReadToEnd() | ConvertFrom-Json; if ($j.tool_input.file_path -like '*.js') {
  prettier --write $j.tool_input.file_path }"

  PostToolUse hook:
  powershell -Command "$j = [Console]::In.ReadToEnd() | ConvertFrom-Json; if ($j.tool_input.file_path -like '*.js') {
  prettier --write $j.tool_input.file_path }"

  To set these up:

  1. First, remove the existing Unix-style hooks using /hooks
  2. Add the new PowerShell hooks above

  You can also save this as a reusable script file format-js.ps1:

  $json = [Console]::In.ReadToEnd() | ConvertFrom-Json
  $filePath = $json.tool_input.file_path
  if ($filePath -and $filePath -like "*.js") {
      prettier --write $filePath
  }

  Then your hook would just be:
  powershell -File C:\Users\SriniAchuthan\.local\bin\format-js.ps1

  Would you like me to create that script file for you?

