> prettier - Popular code formatter

● To add prettier hooks for JavaScript files, run these commands:

  PreToolUse hook (format before writing):
  jq -r '.tool_input.file_path | select(endswith(".js"))' | xargs -r prettier --write

  PostToolUse hook (format after writing):
  jq -r '.tool_input.file_path | select(endswith(".js"))' | xargs -r prettier --write

  You can add these using the /hooks command in Claude Code.

  Make sure prettier is installed:
  npm install -g prettier

  Windows note: The xargs -r command is Unix-specific. On Windows, you might need Git Bash or WSL for these hooks to
  work, or use a PowerShell equivalent.

