> how do I add a matcher

● claude-code-guide(Find hooks matcher config)
  ⎿  Done (4 tool uses · 32.0k tokens · 28s)

● Here's how to add a matcher to your hooks:

  Option 1: Via /hooks command

  1. Run /hooks
  2. Select the hook event (PreToolUse or PostToolUse)
  3. Select "+ Add new matcher…"
  4. Enter the matcher pattern: Write|Edit
  5. Add your command under that matcher
  6. Save to User or Project settings

  Option 2: Edit settings.json directly

  Your hooks config is in ~/.claude/settings.json. The correct format is:

  {
    "hooks": {
      "PreToolUse": [
        {
          "matcher": "Write|Edit",
          "hooks": [
            {
              "type": "command",
              "command": "powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File C:\\Users\\SriniAchuthan\\.local\\bin\\format-js.ps1"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "PostToolUse": [
        {
          "matcher": "Write|Edit",
          "hooks": [
            {
              "type": "command",
              "command": "powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File C:\\Users\\SriniAchuthan\\.local\\bin\\format-js.ps1"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  }

  Matcher patterns

  - "Write" - matches only Write tool
  - "Edit" - matches only Edit tool
  - "Write|Edit" - matches both (regex OR)
  - "*" - matches ALL tools

  Would you like me to check your current settings.json and fix it for you?

